# keys.pdl - what each key of civ-snes DOES: one verb page (CONFIG; the driver holds no verb of its own). The camera keys Y U I O P belong to the board (D152): they are never bound here, the digits are the game's.
# KEYVERB | key (what the player presses) | verb | arg
KEYVERB | up        | move   | n
KEYVERB | down      | move   | s
KEYVERB | left      | move   | w
KEYVERB | right     | move   | e
KEYVERB | pgup      | move   | ne
KEYVERB | pgdn      | move   | se
KEYVERB | end       | move   | sw
KEYVERB | home      | move   | nw
KEYVERB | b         | found  | -
KEYVERB | 1         | build  | warrior
KEYVERB | 2         | build  | settler
KEYVERB | space     | endturn | -
KEYVERB | bracket   | select | next
# RULE rows: poll_ms = how often the driver looks at the relay file; step_ms = the shortest time between two moves (a held arrow repeats; a press inside it is dropped)
RULE | poll_ms | 50
RULE | idle_poll_ms | 120
RULE | step_ms | 100
